course: dictionary
lesson: 15727
title: Transcripts: written copies of spoken words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A transcript is a written copy of words that were spoken. If someone talks in a video, an interview or a recording, a transcript lets you read every word instead of listening. «The teacher printed a transcript of the interview so the class could read it.»
explain: Transcripts help many people. Deaf people can read what was said in a video, and people learning English can follow the words as they listen. «The podcast has a full transcript on its website.» Full means every word is there.
explain: The word has a second meaning, used mainly in the US and Canada. There, a school transcript is an official list of a student's courses and marks. «Amira needed her school transcript for her college application.» Look at the clues: college and application show it is a list of grades, not spoken words.
fact: Transcript is a noun. Its plural is transcripts.
fact: «A transcript of» a speech is a written copy of the words that were spoken.
fact: In courts and on the news, transcripts record the exact words that were said.
fact: In the US and Canada, a «school transcript» shows a student's courses and marks.
fact: Deaf people use transcripts and captions to read what is said in videos.
exercise: «The class read a transcript of the speech.» What is a transcript? | A special kind of pencil | *A written copy of the words that were spoken | A loud sound made by a speaker | A short film with music
exercise: Ben's mum said, «Your school transcript arrived today.» In the US, what does a school transcript show? | A map of the school | *A list of your courses and marks | The names of your friends | Your favourite lunch
exercise: Why do deaf people use transcripts of videos? | So they can skip the lessons | So the video is shorter | *So they can read what was said | So they can hear the music louder
test: «The lawyer asked for the transcript of the court case.» Find and copy the word that names a written copy of spoken words. | lawyer | court | asked | *transcript
test: «The school sent a transcript with Sam's grades.» What does transcript mean here? | A spoken message | A school trip | A kind of drawing | *A list of courses and marks
exam: «The news station published the transcript of the interview online.» What does the transcript show? | The price of the broadcast | *The exact words that were spoken | How long the interview lasted | The camera angles used
